.TH @APP_SLUG_UPPER@ 6 "@RELEASE_DATE@" "@APP_NAME@ @APP_VERSION@" "Games"
.SH NAME
@APP_SLUG@ \- @APP_SUMMARY@
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B @APP_SLUG@
[\fIGODOT-OPTIONS\fR] [\fB\-\-\fR \fIGAME-OPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
King Grumbold the Petty has grievances. Swing the trebuchet, let go at just
the right moment, and bring his neighbours' castles down. There are 36
castles in three realms, seven breakable materials, eight kinds of ammo, and
a castle editor whose castles can be shared as short text codes.
.PP
Tap (or press Space) to start the swing and again to let go; tap once more
in flight for the ammo's trick. Esc pauses, R restarts, Q and E change ammo.
Everything can be rebound under Settings.
.PP
The game never uses the network.
.SH OPTIONS
Options for the game itself go after
.BR \-\- .
.TP
.BI \-\-level= ID
Start straight in the level \fIID\fR, for example \fBgreenmantle-01\fR (it
must be unlocked).
.TP
.BR \-\-screen= levels | settings | editor
Open the level list, the settings or the castle editor.
.PP
Useful engine options go before
.BR \-\- :
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-fullscreen
Start in fullscreen.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-windowed
Start in a window.
.TP
.BI \-\-display\-driver " x11|wayland"
Choose the display server (Wayland is preferred when available).
.TP
.BI \-\-rendering\-method " mobile|gl_compatibility"
Use the OpenGL renderer on hardware without Vulkan.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/@APP_SLUG@/
Progress (save.json), your castles (levels/) and logs.
.TP
.I ~/.config/@APP_SLUG@/settings.cfg
Settings and controls.
.PP
Both follow \fBXDG_DATA_HOME\fR and \fBXDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR when set.
.SH SEE ALSO
@APP_HOMEPAGE@
.SH LICENSE
Code MIT; art, audio, levels and text CC BY-SA 4.0; fonts OFL 1.1. See
/usr/share/licenses/@APP_SLUG@/ (or the same folder under your install
prefix).
